The original-language track is mapped from the source video (0:a:0, -c:a:1 copy) instead of re-encoding data/source-audio.wav: it is lossless, keeps the source codec/bitrate, and the WAV is only a decoded copy of it. The original track's language tag comes from the transcript's detected language, not the source tag, because the sample source mislabels Japanese audio as 'eng'. Subtitles are rebuilt from translation.json segments rather than reusing segments.srt (has [SPEAKER_xx] labels) or subtitles.srt (10-15 s blocks). Burn-in was skipped because the Homebrew ffmpeg has no libass/libfreetype, so it could not be tested.
